:: Lucas Cat Quest 1 [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 15>>
<<set $LucasCat to "Roy">>
While you are unsure of the exact specifics of when you are supposed to meet <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span>, <span style="Color: LightGreen">you luckily arrive just as you see him and his mother walk up to the animal shelter.</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> runs up upon seeing you <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hey, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$LucasNickname</span>! You made it. I was going to remind you during Math, but <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Mr. Randolph</span> was watching us like a hawk today.”</span> He chuckles. <br>

    <<set _ad to [
		{
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
				Mouth: "Happy",
    		},	
        },
        {
            Name: "Lucas",
            State: {
				Outfit: "Everyday",
				Mouth: "Happy",
    		},	
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hello, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span>.”</span> His mom greets you, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I would have picked you up from your house, but <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> didn’t mention we were meeting you until we were already halfway here.”</span> She looks at her son, who chuckles nervously, admitting that he should have run it by her earlier. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It’s fine. I’m going to talk to the shelter workers to find out what we need for our new little family member. You two look around and find one you like, just try not to take too long.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> nods and the three of you walk inside. <br>
<br>
The shelter workers seem happy to see you, excitedly mentioning that they get a lot of stray cat and kittens this time of year. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“We’re working on a spay and neutering program, but the city still has a overpopulation problem. I’m sure we’ll be able to find you’re the perfect new friend!”</span> As you two are led to the cat area, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> asks what ‘spay and neutering’ means and then immediately shivers at the answer. <span style="Color: Yellow">To be fair, the worker goes a bit more detailed than needed.</span> <br>
<br>
As the three of you and the worker move through the shelter, the two of you stop at some of the various rooms and cages. You see a bird and tilt your head at it, examining the plumage of its feathers, only for it to tilt its head as well, mimicking you for a bit as you walk on amused. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span>, surprised to see the shelter has a small collection of large tarantulas, jokingly walks over and asks his mom if he can get one of those. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Haha, no.”</span> She says bluntly before suddenly spying something cute and rushing over to a cage full of small white mice. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oooo! Look at their cute little faces! Why don’t we adopt a mouse, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span>? They’re so cute!”</span> You spy <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> blush a bit at the mice and take a set back nervously. His blush deepens as he notices you looking, trying to play it off like he isn’t a little afraid. You laugh as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Selina</span> is led to another room where she can get information and a list of supplies cooing at some snakes along the way. <br>
<br>
You two walk into the cat area, a large room with a wall of cages, all nicely decorated and designed for comfort. Most of the cages are open, the cats wandering around the large, spacious room. <span style="Color: LightGreen">It’s a far cry from the shelters you’ve seen before, this one much more focusing on making sure the cats are comfortable and well-cared for.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Thankfully, Mayor King has a soft spot for animals, so we get plenty of funding.”</span> The worker laughs when she notices you and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> looking at the room with wide eyes, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Plus we get a ton of volunteers.”</span> <br>
<br>
She runs down the basics. Each cage is assigned to a cat and has some documents about them, from age, birthday, medical conditions, and everything else. Each cat has a collar with their number or name, though most of the kittens don’t have names yet, only numbers, since we like to let the adopters get a chance to name them. You both stand there awkwardly for a moment, watching the dozens of cats of different ages wander around, nap, or being taken care of by the volunteers before eventually starting to look around. <br>


<<linkreplace"<br>Continue">>

    <<set _ad to [
		{
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
				Mouth: "Smirk",
    		},	
        },
        {
            Name: "Lucas",
            State: {
				Outfit: "Everyday",
				Mouth: "Smirk",
                Blush: 1,
    		},	
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Aahhh! They’re all so cute!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> coos. It has been about 5 minutes since you entered, and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> is now sitting on the ground covered in cats. <span style="Color: LightGreen">Kittens nip at his clothes while older cats rub themselves against him, and even an elder cat somehow managed to find its way onto his lap.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Aaahhh, I just want to adopt them all! How can I choose just one?”</span> He sighs as he stands up, placing the cats on him back on the ground and watching as they all scatter about to find something else to give them attention. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Mom said we should get a kitten.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> explains, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“She called the shelter and they said they have so many litters found in town. Plus, with us being so busy, they didn’t think getting an older cat with health problems would be a good idea. Can’t give it the care it needs, you know? Plus, I kinda want one that’s playful and stuff.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> chuckles a little, rubbing the back of his head, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Is that bad of me? I know all cats deserve love, but if I can only get one…”</span> You chuckle, telling <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> he doesn’t need to justify wanting a little kitten. It’s pretty common for kids your age to want a younger animal. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> nods and the two of you continue looking around, however, <span style="Color: Yellow">are startled by the sudden commotion as a small cat manages to dash over the cord of a nearby fan, knocking it over and causing a small panic amongst the felines that leave them running and scrambling in all directions.</span> The perpetrator, a small black cat with bright blue and yellow eyes, doesn’t seem all that bothered by the mess he made until a volunteer calls out <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“That’s the third time you’ve knocked something over today! I think you need to go back in your cage to calm down a little.”</span> <br>
    <br>
    The volunteer suddenly moving towards them is what sends the small kitten off, sprinting away right towards you both! <span style="Color: Yellow">You and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> turn just in time to see the kitten leap onto <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span>’ $LucasBottoms.Type, clawing into them, getting its tiny claws stuck, and flailing around to try and escape until-</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: Pink">Thwomp! <br>

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Smirk",
                    Eyes: "Tired",
                },	
            },
            {
                Name: "Lucas",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Everyday",
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                    Blush: 2,
                    PantsDown: true,
                },	
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

    The cat yanks down <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span>’ bottoms to his ankles, exposing his $LucasUndies.Name! <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> gasps in embarrassment, but before he can even think about pulling them back up, the kitten, still fearful of being punished, rips its claws out and leaps up again, this time latching onto the side of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span>’ underwear! The boy quickly reaches down and grabs the cat before its bodyweight yanks that down as well, exposing his bits to a room full of cats and volunteers.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Woah! H- hold on!”</span> The kitten flails about in his hands, <span style="Color: Pink">causing the boy to lose his balance due to the bottoms around his ankles and fall backwards, landing flat on his butt as the cat tries to bury itself in his shirt, though gets snatched up by the volunteer by the scruff of its neck.</span> The cat seems to nervously look away as the volunteer glares at it in annoyance. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span>, thoroughly embarrassed, quickly fixes his pants as he stands up. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Sorry about him.”</span> The volunteer says as the cat is placed back in its assigned cage, sitting and clawing sadly at the door as if trying to apologize and beg to be let free once more. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“That one is a handful. Runt of the litter but got the energy of a cat twice its size. He’s also a bit of a troublemaker. You’re not the first person he’s pantsed. Starting to think he does it on purpose.”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span>, still blushing a little as he fixes his bottoms, turns and stares at the cat for a minute before smiling. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I think I know which one I want.”</span> He walks up to the cage and looks at the information paper. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“He’s only a few months old. Labeled as energetic, curious, and clingy. Sounds like someone else I know.”</span> He laughs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But no name…”</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Energetic is right.”</span> The volunteer laughs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Sure you can handle that? He’s like a walking tornado.”</span> Despite the warnings, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> seems pretty convinced. He pokes his finger into the cage, asking the cat if he wants to come home with him. The cat, looking a little confused, leans forward to sniff his fingers. <span style="Color: LightGreen">It seems to like what it smells, as it quickly begins to purr and rub its body against his hand, almost looking like its smiling.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yeah. I think he’s the one.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> looks to you and nods. You can’t disagree. <br>
    <br>
    [[Continue|Lucas Cat Quest 2]]
<</linkreplace>>

:: Lucas Cat Quest 2 [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 15>>
The volunteer was a bit worried that getting the small, crazed cat into a carrier to be taken home would be hard, <span style="Color: LightGreen">but much to his surprise, the black kitten doesn’t seem all that opposed to being carried by <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span>.</span> He does try to escape when put in the crate, hissing and scratching, but eventually <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> is able to get him in, though the cat seems to be pouting the entire time as he is carried to the front along with the stuff from his cage, a bed, cushion, and other small things they say they give with the animals since they grow accustomed to it. <br>
<br>
Then comes the paperwork, which isn’t too hard since <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span>’ mom has done most of it by the time you get there. You also can’t help but notice the large amount of cat supplies, litter, and food she suddenly has on a small wagon. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Turns out, they sell this stuff here as a way to raise funds.”</span> She says happily as the volunteer behind her struggles to pull the cart, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Figured why go to some corporate owned slop store when I could get them here. Even if it is more expensive, it goes to a good cause!”</span> <br>

        <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                },	
            },
            {
                Name: "Lucas",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Everyday",
                    Mouth: "Smirk",
                },	
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> rightly points out that she may have went a little overboard, but she waves him off. You wiggle your finger into the crate at the cat as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> and his mom finish up the paperwork. <span style="Color: LightGreen">The cat looks at you with suspicion. You can’t be tell what he feels about you yet and find yourself slightly jealous that he attached himself to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> so quickly, quietly teasing that he’ll have to fight you for <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span>.</span> But then, as they finish up the paperwork, the hard question is posed. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“So, what were you thinking for a name for the little guy?”</span> The volunteer asks, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“We can get you a custom collar here and update his paperwork.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Name?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> blushes, looking to you, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m actually not sure… Well, I did have one random idea.”</span> He chuckles, rubbing the back of his head, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’m not set on it, but for some reason I thought of the name <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Roy</span>. No idea why, he just looks like a <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Roy</span>.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> pauses, thinking for a moment. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“What do you think, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$LucasNickname</span>? Did you have a name in mind?”</span> <br>
<br>

<div id="choice">
	<<link "Roy is perfect<br>">>
	<<replace"#choice">>
        <<set $LucasCat to "Roy">>
        <span style="Color: LightGreen">You say that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Roy</span> is perfect!</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Haha, I don’t know where it came from. Just first thing I thought of when I saw him.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> leans down to the front of the cat, sticking his finger inside as he asks <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“So, what do you think? Does being <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Roy</span> sound good to you?”</span>  <span style="Color: LightGreen">The cat meows loudly, as if to accept his new name proudly. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Haha, I think he likes it. Alright, then from now on your <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$LucasCat Taylor</span>!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> <span style="Color: LightGreen">smiles happily as the cat, wanting more attention, begins to paw at him through the cage, causing him to laugh. Both you and his mother look at him with endearing eyes. He seems very happy.</span> <br>
        <br>
        <<include "Lucas Cat Quest 2.2">>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
	<<link "Suggest a name">>
	<<replace"#choice">>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$LucasCat</span>?”</span> He says the name out loud, thinking it over, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yeah! <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$LucasCat</span>! That’s perfect! What do you think of the name?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> looks into the crate, <span style="Color: LightGreen">leading to the cat meowing as if it accepts the name proudly.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Haha, I think he likes it. Alright, then from now on your <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$LucasCat Taylor</span>!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> <span style="Color: LightGreen">smiles happily as the cat, wanting more attention, begins to paw at him through the cage, causing him to laugh. Both you and his mother look at him with endearing eyes. He seems very happy.</span> <br>
        <br>
