:: Lucas Cat Quest 2.2 [nobr]

/* Intro */
It turns out, choosing the cat and filling out the paperwork that comes with it was the easy part. The hard part is loading the mass amount of supplies his mother bought into their small car. The trunk gets full quick, so more is jammed in the backseat and the passenger seat, <span style="Color: Pink">leading to you and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> having to snug close together in one seat with <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$LucasCat</span> on your lap.</span> While he could have been left in his cage, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> didn’t want to risk him being jolted around and he seems to freak out a little as the car starts, confused by the loud noise. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You know, I never thought we needed a larger car.”</span> His mom laughs nervously as she sees just how loaded the small vehicle is, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Since it just the two of us.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You bought like a year’s supply of litter and food and… whatever this is?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> says glancing into some slightly damp plastic bags, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“We could have started out smaller. Would have been cheaper too…”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Well, we COULD have, but you know I hate shopping.”</span> His mother retorts. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You only hate shopping when it’s stuff we need, like food and soap.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> chuckles, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You LOVE shopping when it’s random stuff online we don’t need.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hey now, I survived 26 years in the film industry! I think I deserve to splurge now and again!”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Or everyday…”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Don’t think I won’t beat your little butt right here in front of your friend, young man.”</span> She says in a humorously threatening tone, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Or, better yet, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span>, pull his bottoms down and give his rude butt a smack for me.”</span> <span style="Color: Pink">You laugh, finding their playful back and forth cute, and say you would if you weren’t squished back here shoulder to shoulder.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Darn, well you have my permission to give him a whack on his bare booty next time he annoys you.”</span> <br>

